        {
          "id": "fd25ef8d-adf4-3b68-87a2-1c45cd261394",
          "content": {
            "id": "fd25ef8d-adf4-3b68-87a2-1c45cd261394",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Tesla sales resume fall in European markets in October",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: Tesla sales plunged in October in a number of European countries.</p><p>It's the latest sign the U.S. electric vehicle maker's struggles in Europe continue.</p><p>Local industry data showed Monday (November 3) the automaker's new car registrations dropped 89% in Sweden.</p><p>They were also down 86% in Denmark, and just under a half in the Netherlands.</p><p>The drop-off comes despite industry-wide sales of fully-electric and plug-in hybrid models rising\u00a0119%.</p><p>Tesla's sales have fallen in Europe this year partly due to a small, ageing line-up of models.</p><p>It also faces rising competition from local competitors and Chinese brands.</p><p>In Denmark, for instance, Tesla was outsold by several Chinese EV companies, including BYD and Xpeng.</p><p>The company has also faced a\u00a0backlash from some European consumers against CEO Elon Musk</p><p>He helped fund Donald Trump's U.S. presidential election victory last year and has supported European far-right parties.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: Tesla sales plunged in October in a number of European countries.</p><p>It's the latest sign the U.S. electric vehicle maker's struggles in Europe continue.</p><p>Local industry data showed Monday (November 3) the automaker's new car registrations dropped 89% in Sweden.</p><p>They were also down 86% in Denmark, and just under a half in the Netherlands.</p><p>The drop-off comes despite industry-wide sales of fully-electric and plug-in hybrid models rising&nbsp;119%.</p><p>Tesla's sales have fallen in Europe this year partly due to a small, ageing line-up of models.</p><p>It also faces rising competition from local competitors and Chinese brands.</p><p>In Denmark, for instance, Tesla was outsold by several Chinese EV companies, including BYD and Xpeng.</p><p>The company has also faced a&nbsp;backlash from some European consumers against CEO Elon Musk</p><p>He helped fund Donald Trump's U.S. presidential election victory last year and has supported European far-right parties.</p></body>",
